Package: sigAudit
Type: Package
Title: Gain Accounting for Multi-Algorithm Search in Omics Prognostics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ziming", "Zhao", email = "13317834871@163.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements reference-adjusted gain accounting for omics prognostic
    modelling. For a candidate pool evaluated on validation and held-out test
    partitions, it computes `Gv` (validation gain over a fixed reference), `Gt`
    (held-out gain) and `Orel = Gv - Gt` (reference-adjusted selection optimism),
    and compares selection rules (argmax, top-k ensembles, resampling remedies)
    on a common task set. It separates selection on a noisy criterion from
    comparison against a weak baseline, and keeps `Oraw` distinct from `Orel`.
